---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Notice"
  description="Draft privacy notice for The OC Events Market website and inquiry forms."
  noindex
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <h1>Privacy Notice</h1>
    <p><strong>Owner and legal review required before production launch.</strong></p>
    <p>
      This draft explains the intended website data flow. It does not replace legal advice and must
      be reviewed against the final hosting, analytics, email, retention, and business practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Information submitted through forms</h2>
    <p>
      The client inquiry form may collect name, email, phone, preferred contact method, event type,
      event date or planning status, city or venue, estimated guest count, working budget, planning
      support needs, and an event description. The vendor form may collect business and contact
      details, service area, web and social links, insurance or license context, introduction, and
      portfolio link.
    </p>

    <h2>How information is intended to be used</h2>
    <p>
      Submitted information is intended only to review and respond to an inquiry, assess potential
      fit, maintain necessary business records, protect the forms from abuse, and operate the
      website. Form content must not be sent to analytics systems.
    </p>

    <h2>Service providers</h2>
    <p>
      The final host, transactional email provider, bot-defense provider, analytics service, and
      their data-processing terms must be inserted here before launch. The current code supports
      Resend and Cloudflare Turnstile only when credentials are supplied.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and rights</h2>
    <p>
      The owner must approve a retention schedule, deletion process, request contact, and any
      California-specific disclosures that apply to the business. No retention period is invented in
      this draft.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      A verified privacy contact email or mailing address is still required. Until it is supplied,
      this notice cannot be treated as launch-ready legal copy.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
